# The language defines itself: a power operator `^` written in ordinary Logos,
# used in the same file, and compiled with f.compile().
#
# An operator is a type read in two halves. Its BARE lines say how its own
# spelling parses: where it binds (parse_rank), which way it associates, and
# what happens when `^` stands on the tape (parse, a body over the parsing
# tape `tape`, building the node as `this`, a fresh ^ it fills by name and
# places with tape[0] = this, then marks constructed itself). Its VALUE block
# says what its NODES hold and how they behave: the operands as named fields,
# the output the parse writes per node, and the run every node shares, the
# bare body that computes the power when a ^ node is used plainly. A field
# read such as (a ^ b).lhs walks into the node and runs nothing.
#
# Shape RULED 19 September 2026 (DESIGN ›The constructor is a field‹): run is
# filled inside the instance block, `shared run = (…)`; a bare `run = (…)`
# would fill ^'s own run, what runs when the type itself is used plainly. The
# instance block's slots are predeclared: every instance block starts with the
# slots type's own declares, unfilled, and the type fills them with `=`, so
# the two halves use one form and no line names a slot type. The seed still runs the 4 September shape
# (tests/fixtures/caret.logos), so `logos import ./identities/power.logos`
# waits on the seed catching up.
^ := type (
    # how the spelling ^ itself parses
    parse_rank = *.parse_rank + 1,       # binds tighter than *
    associativity = right,               # 2 ^ 3 ^ 2 is 2 ^ (3 ^ 2)
    parse = (
        this.lhs = tape[-1],                 # this: a fresh ^ node, its value fields holes (ruled 18 September 2026)
        this.rhs = tape[1],                  # by name, not by position
        this.output = tape[-1]:dyad.type,    # the result follows the base
        tape[0] = this,                      # the constructor places the node it built
        tape.is_constructed[0] = true,       # and says so itself: a write to tape[k] never sets the flag (ruled 19 September 2026)
        tape.remove(1),                      # both operands consumed:
        tape.remove(-1)                      # only the ^ node remains
    ),

    instance = (
        # what every ^ node holds
        lhs := ?,                        # the base: takes the type of the operand written into it
        rhs := i32 ?,                    # the exponent: always an i32, a literal molds to it
        output := type ?,                # what this node yields; the parse above writes it
        # how every ^ node behaves when used plainly: one run for all of them
        shared run = (
            r := this.output 1,          # this: the node the body runs over (ruled 18 September 2026)
            for 0..this.rhs ( r = r * this.lhs ),   # no index needed (ruled 17 September 2026)
            r
        )
    )
),
f := fn (x := i32 ?) -> i32 ( x ^ 3 + 1 ),
f.compile(),
f(2)
